
  @DISTRO_PRETTY_NAME@ live system

  The graphical session starts on its own. From this console:
    @DISTRO_ID@-installer                             graphical installer
    @DISTRO_ID@-installer --config FILE --dry-run      unattended installation (see the docs)
    @DISTRO_CLI@ hardware                             what this computer has
    @DISTRO_CLI@ rescue                               repair an installed system
    nmtui                                             connect to a network

  No graphical session? /tmp/@DISTRO_ID@-live-session.log says why;
  /usr/lib/@DISTRO_ID@/bin/@DISTRO_ID@-live-session tries again, and the
  "safe graphics" boot entry uses software rendering.

  User "@LIVE_USER@" has no password and can use sudo.
  Documentation: @DISTRO_DOC_URL@

